# Git stores text with LF. Keep LF in the working tree too, whatever platform
# the checkout happens on: MARS runs on Linux, and a shell script that arrives
# with CRLF line endings fails there with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Byte-exact inputs and outputs. Feature archives and alignments have to round
# trip untouched -- the regression tests compare them value by value, and a
# line-ending rewrite inside a binary payload would corrupt them silently.
*.npz binary
*.bam binary
*.bai binary
*.whl binary
